       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-22 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Actor Khushbu Sundar Condemns Cyber Harassment and Social Media Hacks</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actor Khushbu Sundar has publicly denounced cyberattacks and personal abuse directed at celebrities, emphasizing that public status does not equate to being public property. She firmly stated that invading the privacy of families or using vulgar language against them is unacceptable, noting she will respond to such insults in kind. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/actor-khushbu-sundar-condemns-cyber-harassment-and-social-me.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This follows a security breach where her official X account was hacked in April, prompting her to alert followers to report suspicious activity. Amid these challenges, Sundar is preparing for her upcoming role in the film Dragon, which features Jr NTR.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief is accurate, though it slightly mischaracterizes the 'Dragon' cast by implying Jr NTR is the sole star of the film based on the provided text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
