       <h1>Amazon Employee Files Lawsuit Alleging Sexual Assault</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>AWS manager Laura Danbom has sued Amazon, alleging senior executive Michelangelo Simonte sexually assaulted her during a 2023 business trip to New York. The lawsuit claims the company failed to properly investigate the incident and created a hostile work environment.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/amazon-employee-files-lawsuit-alleging-sexual-assault.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Danbom alleges Amazon violated Washington’s Silenced No More Act by pressuring her to stay quiet about the assault while maintaining professional contact with the accused. Her attorney, Jay Free, contends Amazon ignored crucial evidence, including DNA evidence provided to police. Amazon has yet to address the specific allegations of failing to properly probe the case or attempting to silence the employee.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Excellent reporting that captures the essence of the lawsuit and the claims made by the complainant.</p>
