     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-22 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ambient AI Startup Nirva Raises $33M for Wearable Pendant</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Nirva has secured a $33 million total investment to launch an ambient AI pendant designed to record only the wearer. The device, which functions as a piece of jewelry, uses voice-model onboarding to filter out surrounding conversations, focusing exclusively on the user’s own speech.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/ambient-ai-startup-nirva-raises-33m-for-wearable-pendant.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Founded by former Meta Reality Labs employees, the company aims to provide personal insights rather than productivity tracking. The $249 wearable, which can be worn as a bracelet, does not store audio data or transcripts after processing. Nirva plans to ship the devices by the end of the year, intending to help users improve self-awareness and self-understanding.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Highly accurate summary of the funding and device functionality. Minor detail: The source states the company was founded in 2025, while the brief omits the founding year.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/22/nirva-raises-33m-for-a-pendant-that-only-listens-to-you/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
