     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-22 · editor 8/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi Faces Political Rows, Cyber Threats, and Civic Chaos</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#National News</span> <span>#Politics</span> <span>#Cybersecurity</span> <span>#Art</span></div>
       <p>A significant political dispute has arisen in Delhi concerning the police handling and detentions during CJP protests, alongside criticism of the central government’s development model. Scrutiny was directed at how protestors were detained, with comparisons drawn to past responses during anti-corruption rallies at Ramlila Maidan. Concerns were also raised about regional economic equity, advocating for broad-based growth across southern states like Tamil Nadu, Andhra Pradesh, and Kerala, rather than concentrating major industrial investments and international sporting events solely in Gujarat. Political leaders responded by accusing critics of political fence-sitting while defending their policy decisions and governance priorities, India Today reported.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/delhi-faces-political-rows-cyber-threats-and-civic-chaos.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, actor Dhanush has signaled intentions to enter Tamil Nadu politics, following actor Vijay's path by organizing fan associations. Amid speculation regarding whether Dhanush will launch his own party or foundation, the AIADMK has extended an invitation, welcoming him if he accepts Edappadi K. Palaniswami as leader. A party representative highlighted Dhanush's popularity among youth and underprivileged communities. Meanwhile, high drama unfolded in the Municipal Corporation of Delhi House, which became a battleground over pollution and the release of funds. A physical scuffle broke out among councillors, involving violent brawls, trading blows, and bags being thrown at a woman leader, leading to the Delhi Mayor being escorted out.</p><p>In technology news, two major cybersecurity scares within twenty-four hours have exposed alarming vulnerabilities. Artificial intelligence discovered critical pre-authentication remote code execution flaws in PHP, the programming language powering a vast majority of websites globally. This prompted urgent global security warnings, precautionary shutdowns of government websites in France and Finland, and warnings from India’s cybersecurity agency, CERT-In. Concurrently, a security lapse was identified in digital certificates from Bengaluru-based eMudhra, where eight intermediate certificates had weak cryptographic keys easily recoverable by researchers.</p><p>In response, technology giants Google and Mozilla moved to block the affected certificates across browsers. Although CERT-In confirmed no malicious exploitation of the compromised keys had been detected, cybersecurity experts urged immediate patch updates and enhanced firewall measures. Adding to the week's events, controversy erupted over visual artist Rehan Vadra’s exhibition at Delhi’s Bikaner House after around 70 photographs, including depictions of recent protests and the Indian tricolour, were removed by venue management before the opening. Management cited breaches of booking guidelines against hosting political conversations, while Rehan stated art knows no political boundary. His parents, Priyanka Gandhi Vadra and Robert Vadra, backed him, questioning the removal of images featuring the national flag, while the venue defended its adherence to institutional policy.</p><p>What to watch: Developments across Delhi politics and national security.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft successfully consolidates the disparate events into a coherent summary, though it covers a large volume of topics that require careful tracking of facts.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/video/cjp-protests-police-detentions-regional-development-spark-face-off-ytvd-3022916-2026-10-22?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
