     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-22 · editor 9/10 · 2 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge conf" title="Reported by Bollywood Hungama, TOI Entertainment">confirmed by 2 sources</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi Police Deny Permission for Diljit Dosanjh's October 30 Concert</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Entertainment</span> <span>#Concert</span> <span>#Delhi</span> <span>#Security</span></div>
       <p>Diljit Dosanjh’s upcoming Delhi concert, part of his Aura India Tour and scheduled to kick off its India leg, has hit a roadblock after the Delhi Police denied permission for his October 30 show at Jawaharlal Nehru Stadium, Bollywood Hungama reported. The Office of the Deputy Commissioner of Police (South District) communicated this decision to ticketing partner BookMyShow, citing security concerns, specific threat-related inputs, and existing law-and-order commitments during the ongoing festive season. Fans are left disappointed, with the denial marking a setback for the Aura India Tour, according to TOI Entertainment.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/delhi-police-deny-permission-for-diljit-dosanjhs-october-30-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The police decision, which also referred to other law-and-order concerns, followed a review of an application submitted by the organisers on October 14. While the nature of the specific threat inputs has not been publicly detailed, reports have previously mentioned security concerns surrounding Diljit, including alleged threats linked to Khalistani elements. However, the police communication does not publicly establish that any particular threat was directed at the singer or the concert. This development unfolds amid wider security concerns in Delhi and recent incidents involving the Lawrence Bishnoi gang, including reports of shots fired outside Diljit’s manager’s residence and an attack involving actor Tiger Shroff.</p><p>The Delhi concert was originally scheduled for November 1 but was later moved forward to October 30. This date change occurred after Rajya Sabha MP Vikramjit Singh Sahney appealed, raising concerns about holding the concert on November 1, the anniversary of the 1984 anti-Sikh violence. The organisers subsequently announced the October 30 date, confirming that existing tickets would remain valid for the rescheduled show. Organizers are now faced with the challenge of possibly seeking new permits or rescheduling the concert, as noted by TOI Entertainment.</p><p>As of October 22, the denial of police permission does not by itself confirm the concert's cancellation. There has been no confirmed announcement from the organisers regarding a new date, an alternative venue, or a complete cancellation of the Delhi show. Reports noted that the event listing continued to appear on BookMyShow, though this does not amount to confirmation of police clearance. Fans who have already purchased tickets await an official update from the organisers and BookMyShow. Separately, Diljit Dosanjh announced an Ahmedabad concert at Narendra Modi Stadium on November 21, following a sold-out Wembley show.</p><p>What to watch: Official updates on the Delhi concert's status.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is thorough, correctly attributing the police decision to the provided sources and accurately summarizing the context of the concert's scheduling issues.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>How this was reported · 2 sources</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/bollywood/diljit-dosanjhs-aura-india-tour-hits-roadblock-as-delhi-police-deny-permission-for-october-30-concert/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/diljit-dosanjh-denied-permission-by-delhi-police-for-his-concert-on-october-30-at-jawaharlal-nehru-stadium-over-security-concerns/articleshow/135114103.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>Synthesised from 2 independent reports on the same event. Details are attributed to the outlet that carried them; nothing outside these sources is published.</p>
    </div>
       
