      <a href="/feed.xml" title="RSS">RSS</a>
      <button id="tdp-theme" title="Toggle light/dark">Light</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <nav class="catrow"><span class="catgrp"><b>News</b><a href="/category/national">national</a><a href="/category/world">world</a><a href="/category/defence">defence</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Money</b><a href="/category/business">business</a><a href="/category/finance">finance</a><a href="/category/education">education</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Sports</b><a href="/category/sports">sports</a><a href="/category/cricket">cricket</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Culture</b><a href="/category/entertainment">entertainment</a><a href="/category/positive">positive</a><a href="/category/funny">funny</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Life</b><a href="/category/science">science</a><a href="/category/environment">environment</a><a href="/category/space">space</a><a href="/category/health">health</a></span><span class="catgrp"><b>Tech</b><a href="/category/tech">tech</a><a href="/category/ai">ai</a></span></nav></div><div class="gtr"><span>Read in your language:</span><div id="google_translate_element"></div></div><div class="wrap"><main id="content"><p class="crumb"><a href="/">← Front page</a> · <a href="/archive">Archive</a> · <a href="/category/science">science</a></p>
     <article class="story single" data-beat="science">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · Phys.org · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Fraunhofer IAF Develops High-Contrast Diamond Quantum Sensor</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Researchers at Fraunhofer IAF have created a laser-enhanced quantum sensor using nitrogen-vacancy centers in diamond that achieves 100% optical contrast. By integrating these centers directly into a laser cavity, the team improved the ratio of magnetic-field sensitivity to dynamic range by up to 590 times.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/fraunhofer-iaf-develops-high-contrast-diamond-quantum-sensor.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This breakthrough utilizes a coherent laser readout signal with power up to 50 mW, significantly outperforming conventional fluorescence-based methods. The technology, detailed in Nature Communications, offers a sensitivity below 400 fT/√Hz, promising advancements in medical diagnostics, navigation, and resource exploration.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Dense and accurate summary of the Fraunhofer IAF quantum sensor breakthrough matching all source details.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://phys.org/news/2026-10-diamond-laser-optical-contrast-magnetic.html" rel="noopener">Phys.org</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
