     <article class="story single" data-beat="health">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">HEALTH</span> · ET Healthworld · 2026-10-22 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>FSSAI issues notices to Nestle, Zydus over 'misleading' claims</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Health</span> <span>#FSSAI</span> <span>#Nestle</span> <span>#Zydus</span></div>
       <p>The Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) has issued notices to Nestle and Zydus concerning what it describes as &quot;misleading&quot; claims made by the companies. This action by the FSSAI underscores its regulatory oversight regarding product advertising in the health sector.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/fssai-issues-notices-to-nestle-zydus-over-misleading-claims.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Specifically, the FSSAI flagged a claim made by Nestle stating that &quot;5 HMOs helps support normal immune system.&quot; The regulatory body expressed concern that this assertion could be interpreted by consumers to mean the product is effective in supporting immunity specifically for a particular physiological condition.</p><p>The FSSAI's intervention highlights the importance of clear and unambiguous communication in product labeling and marketing, particularly for items making health-related claims.</p><p>What to watch: Further actions by FSSAI regarding product claims.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately conveys the FSSAI's position, though it could have been strengthened by mentioning Zydus's specific claims, which are absent from the provided summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://health.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/policy/fssai-issues-notices-to-nestle-zydus-over-misleading-claims/135104062" rel="noopener">ET Healthworld</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
