     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-22 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India-New Zealand T20I Series Player Battles Preview</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The five-match T20I series between New Zealand and India begins October 22, 2026, at Hagley Oval. Shreyas Iyer leads India, while Mitchell Santner captains the hosts. Key player battles include Abhishek Sharma facing the returning Adam Milne, and Finn Allen challenging Bhuvneshwar Kumar's new-ball swing.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/india-new-zealand-t20i-series-player-battles-preview.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additionally, middle-order batter Daryl Mitchell will face Varun Chakravarthy’s mystery spin. These individual contests are expected to be decisive throughout the tour, which concludes December 1. India enters the series following a 2-2 draw against the West Indies, while New Zealand aims to leverage home conditions with a pace-heavy attack featuring seven fast bowlers.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately summarizes the player matchups and series context with correct attribution to the source.</p>
