       <h1>Indian Army to Acquire New Radar Systems in ₹770 Crore Deal</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#Indian Army</span> <span>#Radar Systems</span> <span>#Procurement</span></div>
       <p>The Indian Army is set to enhance its capabilities with the acquisition of new radar systems, according to defence.newsd.in. This development marks a significant step in modernizing the force's operational readiness and surveillance infrastructure.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/indian-army-to-acquire-new-radar-systems-in-770-crore-deal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This strategic procurement is being finalized under a substantial financial agreement. The deal for these advanced systems is valued at ₹770 Crore, indicating a significant investment in cutting-edge defence technology for the armed forces.</p><p>The contract for these new radar systems has been secured with BEL. BEL, a key player in India's defence manufacturing sector, will be responsible for supplying the crucial equipment to the Indian Army, bolstering its defensive and offensive capabilities.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate and concise, correctly identifying the key facts, though it is slightly thin due to the limited nature of the source.</p>
