     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Jain College of Engineering and Research hosts ICCMN‑2026 in Belagavi</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Jain College of Engineering and Research (JCER) in Belagavi began hosting the International Conference on Computing, Communication and Wireless Technology (ICCMN‑2026) on Friday and Saturday. The event features 252 selected papers out of 2,342 submissions, organized into 26 technical tracks and evaluated by 562 reviewers, covering computing, communication, networking, artificial intelligence and emerging technologies.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/jain-college-of-engineering-and-research-hosts-iccmn2026-in-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Speakers from eight countries—including Sri Lanka, Bangladesh, Australia, Thailand, the United States and China—will deliver expert lectures, interactive sessions and discussions. Organizers say the conference will promote knowledge exchange, research collaboration and new technology development, with JCER’s principal S.V. Gorabal emphasizing its role in advancing research, higher education and technical innovation.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate, concise, and includes all key statistics from the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
