       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Kollam district announces Special Summary Revision 2027 schedule</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Kollam District Collector Anie Jula Thomas announced that the Special Summary Revision 2027 draft electoral roll will be published on November 12, with the final list due January 4, 2027. Political parties have been urged to appoint Booth Level Agents at all polling stations to ensure a smooth process. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/kollam-district-announces-special-summary-revision-2027-sche.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Citizens can submit objections from November 12 to December 11, with resolution expected by December 28. Additionally, a 'Campus to Booth' enrolment drive for youth will run from November 2 to November 7, following the conclusion of digital help desk operations on October 31.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate coverage of the electoral revision schedule and administrative requirements.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/special-summary-revision-2027-in-keralam-draft-electoral-roll-to-be-published-on-nov-12-final-list-on-jan-4/article71611576.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
