     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Leaked Mass Effect: Universe Trailer Surfaces Following BioWare Closure</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A trailer for the canceled project 'Mass Effect: Universe' was leaked on Reddit one day after EA shuttered BioWare. Verified by Bloomberg and IGN as legitimate, the footage features in-engine scenes, pre-production assets, and a cameo from a character from the original trilogy.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/leaked-mass-effect-universe-trailer-surfaces-following-biowa.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The game, which focused on an ex-soldier and a mysterious Asari, was in development until the studio's recent closure. Despite the cancellation of this title, reports indicate that Amazon continues to work on a Mass Effect television series for Prime Video.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Succinctly covers the leaked trailer, verification details, and Amazon TV series status.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1016932/mass-effect-5-universe-trailer-leak-bioware-ea" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
