       <h1>Madhya Pradesh Rajya Sabha Bypoll Scheduled for November 12</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission of India has announced a byelection for a Rajya Sabha seat in Madhya Pradesh, following the resignation of former Union Minister L. Murugan. Murugan vacated the seat on October 14, with his original term set to expire in April 2030.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/madhya-pradesh-rajya-sabha-bypoll-scheduled-for-november-12.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Polling and vote counting will occur on November 12, with nominations closing on November 2 and withdrawals on November 5. The election process is slated for completion by November 16. As the BJP currently holds power in the state, its candidate is expected to win the seat easily.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The brief effectively captures the essential details of the by-election, including dates and the context of the vacancy.</p>
