     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Ranbir Kapoor sports Rs 35.88 lakh watch at Ramayana event</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actor Ranbir Kapoor attended a promotional event for the film 'Ramayana' in Hyderabad wearing a bespoke midnight-blue bandhgala paired with a Jacob &amp; Co. Epic X Sher-e-Punjab Gold Edition watch, valued at approximately Rs 35.88 lakhs. The actor’s ensemble also featured a stone-embellished bird brooch and amber-tinted glasses.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/ranbir-kapoor-sports-rs-3588-lakh-watch-at-ramayana-event.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Directed by Nitesh Tiwari, 'Ramayana: Part One' is set for a worldwide theatrical release on November 5, 2026. The film stars Kapoor as Lord Rama, alongside Sai Pallavi as Sita and Yash as Ravana, with a second installment planned for Diwali 2027.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurately captures the promotional event details, watch specifics, and film release information.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/ranbir-kapoor-pairs-a-midnight-blue-bandhgala-with-a-rs-35-88-lakhs-jacob-co-watch-at-ramayana-event-in-hyderabad/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
