       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>SCR Operates 120 Special Trains Carrying Four Lakh Passengers</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>South Central Railway operated approximately 120 special trains to key destinations last week, accommodating nearly four lakh additional passengers during the festival season, General Manager Sanjay Kumar Srivastava announced on Thursday. The zone plans to sustain efforts to meet travel demand through special services and extra coaches.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/scr-operates-120-special-trains-carrying-four-lakh-passenger.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During an inspection of Cherlapalli railway station, Srivastava reviewed circulating areas and approach road works, and engaged with commuters at a &quot;Jan Samvaad&quot; event regarding safety, hygiene, and drinking water. Similar feedback sessions were conducted across the Hyderabad, Secunderabad, and Nanded railway divisions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Well-summarized wire brief containing all core figures and inspection details.</p>
