       <h1>Trump Claims Google CEO Rejected Request to Rename Atlantic Ocean</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>President Donald Trump revealed during a rally at Clemson University that he asked the CEO of Google to rename the Atlantic Ocean. Trump, who has previously renamed two bodies of water after America, stated that the executive pushed back against the proposal.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/trump-claims-google-ceo-rejected-request-to-rename-atlantic-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the President shared his desire to redub the ocean, he did not provide further details on the executive's specific response beyond characterizing it as a rejection. The comment occurred during a South Carolina campaign event where Trump discussed his ongoing efforts regarding geographic naming conventions.</p>
