     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-22 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>UDF Ousts LDF in Upputhara Panchayat With BJP Support</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The United Democratic Front (UDF) has gained control of the Upputhara grama panchayat in Idukki after passing a no-confidence motion against the ruling Left Democratic Front (LDF). The motion passed with 10 votes, bolstered by an unexpected vote from BJP member Nisha Pradeep and the defection of Independent member Ramani Roopesh.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-22/udf-ousts-ldf-in-upputhara-panchayat-with-bjp-support.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Roopesh cited stalled local development as her reason for leaving the LDF coalition. The BJP leadership has stated it will initiate disciplinary action against Pradeep for violating the party whip. The LDF had held power in the panchayat for the past decade, including the last 10 months with Independent support.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Accurate reporting on the political shifting in the panchayat and the specific circumstances of the vote.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/kerala/udf-unseats-ldf-in-upputhara-panchayat-in-idukki-with-bjp-support/article71611616.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
